# {{name}}

A Flare plugin. `manifest.json` declares what it offers; the platform verifies the signed bytes.

```sh
flare-plugin check .
flare-plugin pack . --key publisher.pem --key-id <key id>
flare-plugin publish {{name}}-1.0.0.fpkg --url https://console.example.com
```

Files under `assets/` go into the package, and `pack` lists their digests in the manifest it signs.
Replace the `artifact` placeholders with what your release pipeline built. `check` warns until you do.

Implement the service with `flare-plugin-kit`, following the
[plugin guide](https://github.com/flare-im/flare-plugin-devkit/blob/main/flare-plugin-host/docs/build-your-own-plugin.md).
